{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791617007,"nonce":"3jl8HB6j6nSa8d+f5ft9J+lU4bo=","title":"The inliner rebuilt its whole renaming table for every instruction it copied","message":"inline::substitute_operands converted the `subs` HashMap (each callee value's id to its fresh id in the caller) into a new IndexMap for every instruction it rewrote, so copying a callee of n instructions cost about n squared map insertions; replace_uses_across_function did the same once per instruction of the whole caller. On method_call's lua$chunk the first inline round took 3.4 to 3.7 ms for 15 sites, the second 1.12 ms.\n\nFix: the table is an IdMap (insertion-ordered, Fx-hashed) from the start, which replace_uses takes as it is.\n\nAfter: first round 1.5 to 1.7 ms, second 0.86 ms. Start-up instructions (llvm-backend build, PROFILE_STARTUP=10, median of 3, Mac): Lua 17 benchmarks 26.19G -\u003e 25.38G (-3.1%; op_overload -9.8%, method_call -6.1%, mandelbrot_strip -3.6%, records and tokenize -2.8%, pipeline -2.1%); Python 9 kernels -0.1%. Optimised bodies of 14 Lua benchmarks with ZYNTAX_DISABLE_WARM_UP=1 are byte-identical.","files":null}]}